<Step id="STEP_1_GET_PHASE_CONTEXT">
      <Goal>First action, every phase, every retry: get the manifest from the tool, not from a pasted prompt.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Run phaseContext ToolCall below. Its output IS the phase's working
        context — objective, gates with a satisfy-hint, exit criterion, the phase-scoped
        lifecycle manifest (`READ files` are existing inputs; `CREATE files` are absent write
        reservations and MUST NOT be read before creation), and a `[HANDOFF]` block quoting every completed prior phase's verbatim
        `**Handoff →**` line (absent → this is the first phase). Follow this output for the rest of
        the phase; do not separately open Meta, Phases Overview, or another phase's body — the tool
        already filtered all of that. `ERR_CLI_SDD_TASK_PHASE_NOT_FOUND` → `H_PHASE_NOT_FOUND`; the
        header line's `status=[x]` with no `fix` reason from the dispatch → `H_PHASE_ALREADY_DONE`;
        an Input that should cite a prior phase but has no matching `[HANDOFF]` entry →
        `H_INPUT_HANDOFF_MISSING`.
        <ToolCall owner="phase-worker" result="phaseContext">npx gennady sdd-task <ticket> --phase <PhaseID></ToolCall> Inputs <ticket>, <PhaseID>: <ticket> and <PhaseID>=exact activation values supplied by execute STEP_2. Use phaseContext.
      </Action>
    </Step>